Nethack's intended to be played without such a safety net:if you die,
you start a new game.  It would be incredibly boring and easy if you
could just restore if you died, and there are plenty of game features
that would become totally broken if that were possible (e.g. if
something has a 5% chance of granting a wish, you could try it and
restore repeatedly until you got the wish, and you could easily wind
up with multiple bones files left by the same character).

As others have mentioned, there's a "God mode" called explore mode if
you just want to see how the later game works without any chance of
dying, but it's not much like really playing the game.


